WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:09.580
Picture New York City and you’re probably
thinking about Midtown

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:13.420
Time Square, the Empire State Building, Grand
Central….

00:00:13.420 --> 00:00:15.260
This is Midtown Manhattan

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:22.970
Tourist flock to it, while locals often try
- and fail - to avoid it

00:00:22.970 --> 00:00:28.580
But there is more to this part of town than
tourist traps and traffic congestion

00:00:28.580 --> 00:00:34.550
Midtown has been electrified by a bolt of
Brooklyn Hip and Wall Street money.

00:00:34.550 --> 00:00:37.420
Maybe it's time you took a second look

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:48.020
Midtown is everything between 14th street
and Central Park South

00:00:48.020 --> 00:00:52.710
It is the world’s largest central business
district

00:00:52.710 --> 00:00:56.050
It also has some of the most expensive real
estate

00:00:56.050 --> 00:01:00.430
And it doesn’t get any ritzier than Fifth
Avenue which commands the world's highest

00:01:00.430 --> 00:01:01.420
retail rents

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:10.040
But if there is one building more responsible
than any other for midtown’s success

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:11.300
it's this one

00:01:15.490 --> 00:01:21.920
Built in 1913, Grand Central Terminal helped
sparked a boom in construction that made Midtown

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:25.070
the center of American capitalism

00:01:25.070 --> 00:01:30.920
This audacious building is used by more than
one million people a week.

00:01:30.920 --> 00:01:37.100
A century after it was built it has only now reached capacity. That’s future proofing

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:46.470
New York embraces eating out. There are over
45 thousand restaurants in the city

00:01:46.470 --> 00:01:53.400
It would take 125 years to eat in every one
- not saying your should

00:01:56.340 --> 00:02:00.390
Here in Midtown - the restaurant scene is
embracing change

00:02:00.390 --> 00:02:03.180
A number of Brooklyn institutions have jumped
the river

00:02:07.180 --> 00:02:12.720
Roberta’s pizza started on the other side
of the East River in 2008 but their second

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:16.980
outpost is based in Urbanspace food hall - smack
dab in Midtown

00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:26.040
You could be fooled into thinking this is
Williamsburg not Park Avenue

00:02:29.060 --> 00:02:34.910
Another Brooklyn import is Ichiran, the Japanese
ramen chain whose first US restaurant opened

00:02:34.910 --> 00:02:38.340
in Bushwick in 2016
.

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:44.090
Here you can sit with a group or…. in splendid
isolation in one of the so called ‘flavour

00:02:44.090 --> 00:02:48.020
concentration booths’. Very serious

00:02:50.120 --> 00:02:55.010
But if you want to swap Brooklyn cool for
something a bit more luxury

00:02:55.010 --> 00:02:56.550
we've got the spot

00:02:56.550 --> 00:03:02.340
The Office is an intimate speakeasy offering
pre-Prohibition style cocktails and a food

00:03:02.340 --> 00:03:03.480
menu to match

00:03:05.440 --> 00:03:14.220
You’ll find it hidden away on the 35th floor
of the super swanky Mandarin Oriental

00:03:14.220 --> 00:03:21.470
This is one of the most expensive hotels in
New York, rooms start at $1000 a night

00:03:21.470 --> 00:03:29.300
But there are 113 other hotels in Midtown
offering plenty of choices

00:03:29.300 --> 00:03:33.940
So forget the old wisdom that the excitement
is basically, anywhere but Midtown

00:03:33.940 --> 00:03:37.090
.
This part of Manhattan has something new and

00:03:37.090 --> 00:03:40.640
exciting to offer, whether it’s high end
or rough-and-ready.

